+  "addressing": "Addresses are bare dotted strings, not a tree with an explicit root/mount mechanism. `Part` is defined as \"A semantic PxC address. Identity is the address, not the current value.\" (19b9b92:packages/quick_anno_py/chainspot_quick_anno/core.py:13). `Calculation` enforces one prefix rule only: \"Calculation address must start with 'fn.'\" (19b9b92:packages/quick_anno_py/chainspot_quick_anno/core.py:33-34); Part addresses carry no equivalent enforced rule at all \u2014 any string passes `Part.__post_init__` as long as it's non-empty (core.py:17-19). In practice this tip uses three observed prefix families by convention only, never validated in code: `px.*` for durable stage-produced state (`px.tees.rings.candidates`, `px.tees.family.measured`, `px.tees.family`, `px.tees`, `px.tees.px` in s3.py:33-37; `px.badges.objects`, `px.badges.px`, `px.badges.muted` in s1.py:33-35), `scratch.*` for PCR-derived investigation output (`scratch.s3.rejectedCandidates`, `scratch.s3.visibleTeeSummary` in s3.py:38-39; `scratch.s1.ownershipSummary` in s1.py:35), and `fn.*` for Calculation identity (`fn.quickAnno.s3.summarizeVisibleTees` in s3.py:56). PQL treats prefix matching as first-class: \"Exact Parts and address prefixes are first-class; refinement stays ordinary Python.\" (19b9b92:packages/quick_anno_py/chainspot_quick_anno/pql.py:20), implemented as `PQL.prefix(prefix)` doing `address.startswith(prefix)` over `pxc.items()` (pql.py:37-47) \u2014 i.e. mounts/scoping exist only as a runtime string-prefix query, not as a declared address-space structure. There is no `namespace`, `mount`, or `root` concept anywhere in this surface (grep across experiments/quick-anno-python and packages/quick_anno_py returns zero hits for \"namespace\" or \"mount\"; the only \"root\" hits are the filesystem repo root, e.g. s1.py:8 `ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]`). Nothing in this tip states or implements the owner's \"connection\" principle \u2014 no discussion of what a ro