+  "viewer_and_pcr_render": "The `PrincipleComponentRender` shape from origin.md is directly instantiated as literal JSON keys in `graph.py`'s authoring-only `Pcr.to_pcr_dict()`: `return {\"PrincipleComponentRender\": self.name, \"Ticks\": ticks}` (19b9b92:packages/quick_anno_py/chainspot_quick_anno/graph.py:111), each Tick holding `{\"name\": tick, \"Calculations\": calculations}` (graph.py:110) \u2014 this matches origin.md's `PrincipleComponentRender -> Tick[]`, `Tick -> Calculation[]` shape exactly, but `graph.Pcr` is explicitly non-executing: \"This deliberately does not execute ChainSpot calculations... Execution remains owned by ChainSpot/PxC.\" (graph.py:31-33). The executable sibling, `pcr.PCR` (pcr.py), does run and produces `TickTestimony(name, calculations: tuple[CalculationTestimony,...])` per Tick (pcr.py:68-71) and a `PcrRun(pcr, ticks, results)` (pcr.py:74-78) \u2014 but there is no receipt object, no `observe` flag, no `result_sha256`, no `shadowed_inputs`, and no digest anywhere in this pcr.py (absent by comparison with pyto's `pcr.py:95-128` cited in tick-observability-ledger.md section 3 \u2014 this quick_anno PCR is strictly simpler and keeps full values in `PcrRun.results`, never digesting them: `results[invocation.id] = value` (pcr.py:162) with no digest step). What a person actually sees is not the PCR/testimony JSON but the neon PNG sheet: `materialize_s3_neon.py` composites six fixed panels \u2014 ring candidates (cyan), enclosing frames (orange) plus accepted family (green), accepted visible Tee objects (green boxes + magenta center crosses), exact TeePx in \"18 readable local-context crops\" (magenta halo over dimmed crop, `exact_local_crops`, materialize_s3_neon.py:52-84), the actual remaining raster with TeePx punched transparent over checkerboard (`remaining`, materialize_s3_neon.py:97-107), and rejected/not-accepted categories in red/yellow/orange (`rejected_panel`, materialize_s3_neon.py:110-127) \u2014 assembled by `sheet()` into on