+  "what_it_is": "A checkpoint of the \"quick_anno\" experiment: a small first-class Python PxC/PCR/Part/Calculation/Tick/PQL core (packages/quick_anno_py/chainspot_quick_anno/{core,pcr,pql,graph}.py) plus a driver (experiments/quick-anno-python/s1.py) that shells out to the real TS ChainSpot runtime (export_s1_snapshot.cjs, using the built @chainspot/alg S0/S1 stage contracts) to get a real S1 snapshot for Dash's Track, loads Badge/owned/muted Parts into the Python PxC, runs a tiny Python PCR (\"S1.quick-anno\") that publishes a derived scratch Part, queries it back with PQL, emits a Mermaid view of the composition, and produces a 7-panel \"neon-first\" correctness contact sheet with Pillow (materialize_s1_neon.py). It supersedes an earlier, purely-authoring proof (experiments/quick-anno-python/README.md, base b5a6ae0) that only emitted PCR JSON + Mermaid without touching real data. This is exactly the tree the pyto research docs already cite as `pyto/reference/chainspot-quick-anno/*` (tick-observability-ledger.md rows 3-4, 25-28), so the port pyto is currently doing has this ChainSpot commit as its literal source.\n\nCaveat on `git diff --stat main 82f8fc9`: the archive-fetched `82f8fc9` has no recorded parent in this shallow clone (`git show -s --format=%P 82f8fc9` returned empty) and `git merge-base main 82f8fc9` fails \u2014 the two tips are unrelated grafted histories in this shallow fetch, not a normal feature-branch diff. The stat (1305 files changed, 158602 insertions/139825 deletions) is effectively a whole-tree comparison against a different, mostly-disjoint snapshot of the same repo, not a scoped PR diff \u2014 I read it as confirmation that this is a large, long-lived working tree rather than as a semantic diff, and instead scoped this report to the files under experiments/quick-anno-python/, packages/quick_anno_py/, and the production files they call into.",
