+  "viewer_and_pcr_render": "The tip's Python side has no viewer of its own \u2014 it only emits data (`to_pcr_json`, `to_mermaid`) for later rendering (`f3ecab3:experiments/quick-anno-python/README.md:16-19`). The real viewer/PCR-render evidence in this commit lives on the TS/Svelte side it mirrors, and it matches the owner's \"PCRs are Kibana\" framing precisely: `f3ecab3:packages/alg/src/exec/pcr.ts:17-21` \u2014 \\\"Storybook-facing composition of already-executed Tick testimony. PCR has deliberately no run() method: the production gateway is the only execution authority and hands this function the receipts it already produced.\\\" `pcr.ts:90` further separates render identity from run identity: \\\"View identity is a pure projection of a frozen PCR; it cannot execute CV,\\\" implemented as `pcrRenderId(pcr, viewArgs)` hashing `{runResultId, viewArgs}` \u2014 changing `viewArgs` (zoom, materializationView, showGrid, etc.) changes only the render hash, never the underlying `runResultId`. This is asserted directly in the test suite: `f3ecab3:tests/unit/pcr.test.ts:50,63-72` \u2014 describe block \\\"PCR composes testimony without becoming an engine\\\"; test \\\"changing View Args changes only render identity\\\" asserts `pcrRenderId(pcr,{zoom:2}) !== pcrRenderId(pcr,{zoom:4})` while `pcr.runResultId` is unchanged; test at `pcr.test.ts:74-133` \\\"changing Run Args crosses the production gateway before PCR composition\\\" shows a Run-Arg change (a threshold) must re-execute through the gateway (`gatewayRuns` increments) and produces a different `runResultId`, whereas View Args never do; `pcr.test.ts:51-60,135-139` assert `'run' in pcr === false` and that PCR throws if asked to present \\\"a planned Tick that never ran.\\\" What a person actually sees, per Tick: `f3ecab3:src/lib/evidence-workbench/PcrInspectionHost.svelte` renders one Tick at a time (`TickInspection` component, line 86) with a `materializationView` selector whose full vocabulary is fixed in `f3ecab