+  "addressing": "Root/prefix rule, enforced mechanically: every graph node must be `fn.*` or `px.*` or the compiler rejects it (b5a6ae0:packages/alg/src/stages/S0/exp/mermaid-pcr/compiler.ts:32, :46-47). Addresses are dotted paths that encode stage, experimental-vs-clean status, module and kind before the leaf name, e.g. a per-module ROOT constant: `const ROOT = 'px.s1.exp.maskComponents.part.' as const;` (b5a6ae0:packages/alg/src/stages/S1/exp/mask-components/index.ts:8), used to build every Part's own `address` field (`type PartAddress = \\`px.s1.exp.maskComponents.part.${string}\\`;`, index.ts:21). Each segment discriminates (stage S1, `exp` marking non-canonical experimental status, the owning module `maskComponents`, the kind `part`) rather than being generic \u2014 the closest concrete instance found of the owner's \"meaningful root/segment\" rule, though no file states the rule itself; it is only enacted in code. S1's public output surface is a frozen, named list rather than a wildcard: `export const S1_OUTPUT_ADDRESSES = ['px.badges.objects','px.badges.px','px.badges.muted','px.remaining.afterBadges'] as const;` (b5a6ae0:packages/alg/src/stages/S0/exp/mermaid-pcr/compare.ts:3-7), and `outputAddresses` parity is checked against exactly that set. Cross-Stage alignment is a first-class field, not inferred: every raster Part carries `coordinateFrameId: typeof S0_CROPPED_IMAGE_ADDRESS` (mask-components/index.ts:31) pinning it to the address of the frame it was measured in, plus `sourceAddress`/`sourceTickId` provenance fields. No dynamic registration of addresses at runtime was found in this tip: the graph source (S0.mmd/S1.mmd) is the sole author of which addresses exist, compiled once into YAML (`compileMermaidPcr`), and the interpreter (runner.ts) only reads/writes addresses the compiler already validated \u2014 \\\"declaration order is executable order; reject forward dependencies, including via PxC\\\" (compiler.ts:58 comment). No `mount`, or PxC-storage-backend-selection-by-prefix language was found tied to addressing in this tip's added docs/code (the two `namespace` hits, in scripts/chainspot-lab/README.md:185 and .task/LAB-SCOPE-V0.md:102, are about UI \\\"Search Page\\\" overlay namespaces on a raster, unrelated to px./fn. addressing) \u2014 missing.",
+  "viewer_and_pcr_render": "This tip contains a working embodiment of \"PCRs are Kibana\": a `Pcr` type (packages/alg/src/exec/pcr.ts) that is explicitly a view-only projection with no execution power: \"Storybook-facing composition of already-executed Tick testimony. PCR has deliberately no run() method: the production gateway is the only execution authority and hands this function the receipts it already produced.\" (b5a6ae0:packages/alg/src/exec/pcr.ts:17-21), and `pcrRenderId` is documented \"View identity is a pure projection of a frozen PCR; it cannot execute CV.\" (pcr.ts:90). `composePcr(spec, plan, testimony)` (pcr.ts:51-88) assembles `{schema:'chainspot-pcr@1', id, title, planFingerprint, paramsHash, runResultId, runResultIdentityScope:'tick-testimony-and-materializations', runResultIdentityLimitation:'opaque PxC output values require an emitted Materialization', ticks}` \u2014 the render definition is versioned (`schema`) and honestly scoped, stating what it does NOT prove identity over. Per Tick, a person sees (src/lib/evidence-workbench/TickInspection.svelte): an identity strip of `paramsHash`, `planFingerprint`, `runResultId` plus the honesty caveat rendered inline (`{pcr.runResultIdentityScope}</strong> \u2014 {pcr.runResultIdentityLimitation}`, TickInspection.svelte:55); \"Exact PxC inputs\" as `tick.actualConsumes` addresses with a warning line for anything `declared but unread` (TickInspection.svelte:60-67); \"Calculation identity\" as `frozenCalculations` \u2014 address, `identityScope`, SHA-256 `implementationHash`, and its own limitation string rendered per-row, \"Not transitive: {calculation.limitation}\" (TickInspection.svelte:76-77); \"Exact PxC outputs\" (`tick.writes`) tagged `replacement` when a write collides with a prior address (TickInspection.svelte:86-92); a \"Materializations emitted by this Tick\" section listing each artifact's kind/id/SHA-256/dims or, if none, the explicit line \"No persisted Materialization at this boundary. PxC