+  "storage": "No DuckDB anywhere in this tip \u2014 a repo-wide grep of every added/changed file for \"duckdb\" (case-insensitive) returned zero hits, consistent with pyto's `{?} WarmupBudget` finding (DuckDB's 5.3s warm cost) not being revisited here. What this tip does add is a pluggable, content-addressed artifact/receipt sink abstraction (packages/alg/src/exec/sink.ts, node-sink.ts): `export interface ExecSink { putArtifact(kind, id, bytes, dims?): ArtifactRef; putReceipt(receipt): void; }` (sink.ts:13-16), with three swappable implementations \u2014 `createNullSink()` (hashes/stores nothing, \"the trace-off fast path\", sink.ts:18-19), `createMemorySink()` (\"the browser-safe default. Collects everything for the caller to inspect or hand to its own storage\", sink.ts:34) computing `sha256 = sha256HexSync(bytes)` and `uri: \\`memory://${id}\\`` (sink.ts:44-45), and `createNodeSink(outDir)`, explicitly \"the ONLY file in exec/** allowed to touch node:fs/node:path\", writing deterministically: \"artifacts land under <outDir>/artifacts/<kind>/<id>.bin, receipts are appended one JSON object per line to <outDir>/receipts.jsonl. Deterministic given a deterministic outDir + plan: same plan, same inputs, same bytes on disk every run.\" (node-sink.ts:4-9), with the same sha256-per-artifact (node-sink.ts:25) and `uri: \\`file://${filePath}\\`` (node-sink.ts:30). `ArtifactRef` is documented as a \"Content-addressed reference to an artifact the sink has stored. `uri` is sink-defined ... the exec core never interprets it, only carries it through the receipt.\" (contract.ts:90-95), and dimensions are opt-in, never inferred: \"A consumer receiving undefined MUST NOT infer dimensions from byte length -- decline to rasterize instead.\" (contract.ts:110-111). This is a working instance of pyto's `{?} StorageKinds` thesis (a facade with a kind-selected backend, \"precise opposite of S3\") \u2014 but keyed by a declared artifact `kind` enum (rgba, mask, scalarField, componentSet, badgeEvidence, m1/m2Representation, polyline, measurementTable; contract.ts:77-88) and by explicit sink choice, not by address prefix. Receipts are append-only JSONL, not a single retained.json or any database. No other storage backend (sqlite, a graph store, etc.) appears in this tip.",
+  "materialization_and_ticks": "Two independent Tick-execution mechanisms are present. (1) The production-shaped one, `executeCompiledPlan`/`executeCompiledPlanAsync` (packages/alg/src/exec/gateway.ts:124-219): for each `OperationSpec` it freezes calculation identity via `freezeCalculations` \u2014 hashing `Function.prototype.toString.call(binding.calculate)` into `implementationHash` and erroring loudly if bound calculations disagree with declared `fn.*` addresses (gateway.ts:57-81); tracks real access with `trackAccess(board, op)` yielding `{tracked, consumed, produced, writes}`; times each op (`durationMs = now() - startedAtMs`); throws on declared-vs-actual mismatch only when `op.accessConformance === 'exact'` (`assertAccessConformance`, gateway.ts:103-122) \u2014 conformance checking is opt-in per operation, not global; computes generic \"shape probes\" \u2014 \"for every slot an operation actually produced, record its element count when the value is array-like\" (gateway.ts:83-91, `shapeProbes`), a disclosed partial telemetry (\"fine-grained score distributions still ride ctx.measure/UnitTrace at unit level; Receipt.probes carries op-level candidate-count shape instead.\", gateway.ts:90-91); and extracts artifacts through injected `artifactExtractors`, written via the sink. (2) The experimental one built for this proof, `executeMermaidYaml` (packages/alg/src/stages/S0/exp/mermaid-pcr/runner.ts:27-56), explicitly marked non-canonical: \"Experimental interpreter for compiler output. Actual values remain in the returned record, never in a PxC run-record address. This is not yet the shared PQL executor.\" (runner.ts:25-26). It walks compiled Ticks/Calculations in order, rejects duplicate occurrence ids (\"Duplicate occurrence '${calculation.id}'.\", runner.ts:36), enforces argument/binding non-collision (\"Argument shadows '${name}'.\", runner.ts:38) \u2014 resolving pyto's `{?} SilentRules` shadow concern the loud-failure way JS already does \u2014 and on failure raises `MermaidExecutionError` carrying the partial `RunRecord` with every prior call's status intact (runner.ts:20-24, 49-52), which `run.ts` persists to `failed-run.v8` + `failure.json` on catch (run.ts:47-51), retaining the successful prefix exactly as pyto's Day 2 replay/tamper discipline wants. Materialization proper (turning run values into inspectable files) happens only in the CLI, not the library: `run.ts` pulls `px.course.canonicalPixels`, `px.badges.px`, `px.badges.muted`, `px.remaining.afterBadges` back out of PxC by address and writes them as PNGs (run.ts:26-39), plus a binary V8-serialized trace (\"Binary trace retains typed arrays and shared object identity without giant JSON arrays.\", run.ts:24) and a JSON `receipt.json`. Neither mechanism nor the checklist claims this ran: REFINE.md's checklist is entirely unchecked (\"- [ ] Compile S0 and S1 independently...\", REFINE.md:7-24), stating \"Not completed by this prototype: shared PQL integration, Stage selection/routing, browser traversal, S2 compatibility or promotion.\" (REFINE.md:26-28).",
+  "receipts_and_telemetry": "The canonical receipt shape (packages/alg/src/exec/contract.ts:127-141) is: `interface Receipt { opId; frozenCalculations: FrozenCalculation[]; startedAtMs; durationMs; declaredConsumes; declaredProduces; actualConsumes; actualProduces; writes: PxWriteTestimony[]; probes: Probe[]; artifacts: ArtifactRef[] }`, commented: \"Per-operation execution record. `declared*` comes from the OperationSpec; `actual*` comes from what the operation really touched on the evidence board while running. The two diverging is a conformance failure the gateway surfaces rather than silently accepting.\" (contract.ts:121-125). `FrozenCalculation` self-limits its own claim: `identityScope: 'runtime-function-body'` with `limitation: 'called helpers, constants, templates, and assets are not covered'` (contract.ts:60-67) \u2014 the same limitation pyto's ULTRACODE-WEEK plan already names for `implementation_sha256` (`{?} CacheInvalidation`). `PxWriteTestimony.kind` is a closed union `'new-address' | 'refinement' | 'replacement'` (contract.ts:71-74), making a colliding write a distinguishable, visible event rather than a silent overwrite \u2014 directly answering part of pyto's open `{?} SilentRules`. `Probe { name: string; value: number }` (contract.ts:116-119) is the entire telemetry unit: one named scalar per probe, populated today only by `shapeProbes`' array-length heuristic (gateway.ts:92-101) \u2014 telemetry here is shape-of-output counts, not timing distributions or perceptual scores. The concrete on-disk receipt this commit exercises is `review/s1-ownership/receipt.json`, shaped `{rule, reviewMarginPx, marginPurpose, partition, source, executionMs, owned, muted, remaining, total, perBadge:[{id, number, bbox, components, unaccountedButOwned, excluded}, ...]}` (b5a6ae0:review/s1-ownership/receipt.json:1-29+) \u2014 an accounting receipt (pixel counts that must sum and partition exhaustively), not the `Receipt`/`Tick` shape above; its README states the limit