+  "what_it_is": "An orphan archive commit (725 files, all insertions, sharing no history with main -- which is why `git diff --stat main 8cdddec` reports 1283 files as a symmetric diff between unrelated trees, not a normal commit's diff). It preserves byte-for-byte the local `lab/parts-inspector` checkout at 38ca7ab: a DuckDB-Wasm SQL query surface laid over one completed ChainSpot S1 PQL run, wired to a pixel Part inspector. Sam killed the branch because measured browser startup (5.79s) exceeded the 5s CV budget; no replacement backend shipped. This is the concrete experiment behind pyto/questions.md's {?} WarmupBudget (\"DuckDB was tried and archived because it took 5.3 s to warm, slower than the target\"). It also happens to contain, unmodified, the exact ChainSpot PQL/PCR/PxC reference implementation (packages/alg/src/exec/*) that pyto's origin.md and ULTRACODE-WEEK.md describe transferring to Python, plus a working per-Tick viewer (TickInspection.svelte) that is the closest thing in either codebase to \"PCRs are Kibana\" already built and rendering.",
